@1 = ~A floating piece of armor stands before you. He does not move an inch, and even though he does not have any eyes, you feel as if his gaze sees right through your soul. It looks like he's been assigned to guard the menagerie.~
@2 = ~Hi. Can you understand me?~
@3 = ~Why are you guarding this place? Durlag is gone.~
@4 = ~This dragon...~
@5 = ~I saw a Mind Flayer upstairs. I understand doppelgangers, but why would a Mind Flayer be here?~
@6 = ~How do I get to the lower floors?~
@7 = ~Can you transport me back outside?~
@8 = ~Words... processed. Intent... evaluated. You are not a shapeshifter. You possess a pulse. You are... tolerated. Speak your purpose.~
@9 = ~Why are you guarding this place? Durlag is gone.~
@10 = ~This dragon...~
@11 = ~I saw a Mind Flayer upstairs. I understand doppelgangers, but why would a Mind Flayer be here?~
@12 = ~How do I get to the lower floors?~
@13 = ~Can you transport me back outside?~
@14 = ~The Clanless Master is absent. The Master's order remains. We guard the Menagerie. We guard the Great Trophy. Until the stone turns to dust, or until the core of our steel rusts through... we watch.~
@15 = ~Hi. Can you understand me?~
@16 = ~This dragon...~
@17 = ~I saw a Mind Flayer upstairs. I understand doppelgangers, but why would a Mind Flayer be here?~
@18 = ~How do I get to the lower floors?~
@19 = ~Can you transport me back outside?~
@20 = ~Mechezarin. Great Wyrm of the Earthspur. Bound in iron. Broken in dark. The Master brought him here to show the world the might of the Trollkiller. He hated his cage. He hated his withered wings. But in the end... he hated the skin-stealers more. His bones form the spine of this floor. Durlag died, and no one was left to feed Mechezarin... so he died too. Of starvation.~
@21 = ~Hi. Can you understand me?~
@22 = ~Why are you guarding this place? Durlag is gone.~
@23 = ~I saw a Mind Flayer upstairs. I understand doppelgangers, but why would a Mind Flayer be here?~
@24 = ~How do I get to the lower floors?~
@25 = ~Can you transport me back outside?~
@26 = ~The mind-eater... the master of the shadows. The shifting beasts had a shepherd. They did not possess the cunning to bypass the Master's wards alone. Tentacles guided them. A mind of slime and psychic rot orchestrated the nightmare that broke the Master's sanity. It feasts on the residual madness still echoing through these walls. It hides in the upper darkness, bloated on the clan's ancient fear.~
@27 = ~It isn't the only peril here. Lower... demonic entity, born of pure evil. He is the new master. Cleanse this place if you will. He did not break the Master's family—he merely walks upon the ruins they left behind.~
@28 = ~Hi. Can you understand me?~
@29 = ~Why are you guarding this place? Durlag is gone.~
@30 = ~This dragon...~
@31 = ~How do I get to the lower floors?~
@32 = ~Can you transport me back outside?~
@33 = ~Four chambers... four dominions ruled by masters. Challenges await any brave souls willing to endure them. Defeat the magical rulers of each dominion... you shall pass the test.~
@34 = ~Hi. Can you understand me?~
@35 = ~Why are you guarding this place? Durlag is gone.~
@36 = ~This dragon...~
@37 = ~I saw a Mind Flayer upstairs. I understand doppelgangers, but why would a Mind Flayer be here?~
@38 = ~Can you transport me back outside?~
@39 = ~Yes.~
@40 = ~Take me back outside.~
@41 = ~I'll let you know if I want out.~
